# The helper PC's own values (two-PC setup; README, "Two-PC setup"): ~/.config/localllm/helper.env on the MAIN PC
# (mode 600, in the settings backup). The helper never reads it: ./localllm.sh install-helper and deploy send what it
# needs. ./localllm.sh install-helper makes this file from the template when it doesn't exist yet.

# The helper's folder for everything large (Python environments, models, Open WebUI's data), on one of its internal
# drives. Unset: install-helper picks the internal NTFS drive with the most free space and writes it here, so every
# later run (and a rebuild from the backup) uses the same place. To move it later: README, "Two-PC setup".
# HELPER_DATA_DIR="X:\LocalLLM"

# Optional parts (on or off; on when unset). Off removes the service on the next install-helper.
# HELPER_SMALL_MODEL="on"   # a small model for Open WebUI's chat titles, tags and follow-up questions
# HELPER_IMAGES="on"        # ComfyUI with Stable Diffusion 1.5, for images in Open WebUI
# HELPER_DOCLING="on"       # Docling, which reads PDFs and scans (with OCR) for Open WebUI's documents

# Kokoro (text-to-speech) on the helper's gpu (default) or cpu.
# HELPER_KOKORO_DEVICE="gpu"
